  "proof_scope": "For a finite normal surface with finite disjoint trace arcs joining distinct sides of each normal disk, a zero-edge-weight cut patch with b proper original-boundary arcs has Euler characteristic b/2+sum(1-k_j/2), k_j>=2. Hence diskpatches with b=0 or1 have positive edge weight. No orientability, irreducibility, RP\u00b2 exclusion or choice hypothesis.",
  "use": "Supplies positivity needed when choosing least-weight disk patches in reduced normal-sum/exchange arguments. Does not assert fundamental/vertex disk existence or resolve nonseparating-sphere exchange obstruction.",
